    {
      "id": "months-and-dates",
      "number": "85",
      "heading": "The Months and the Date",
      "statement": "The Lithuanian months are **native words**, not the international ones, and most of them name what the country is doing or what the weather is doing — *birželis* is the birch month, *rugpjūtis* the rye-cutting. A date is the **genitive** of the month followed by the ordinal of the day: *sausio penkta*, the fifth of January, literally *January's fifth*.",
      "paradigms": [
        {
          "caption": "The twelve months",
          "columns": [
