    {
      "id": "the-year",
      "number": "86",
      "heading": "The Year",
      "statement": "A year stands in the **instrumental plural** with *metais*, and only the **last** element of the number is made an ordinal. This is the one construction of the level that looks alarming written out, and it is entirely mechanical: read the number as a cardinal until the final word, make that an ordinal, and put both into the instrumental plural.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "target": "Gimiau tūkstantis devyni šimtai devyniasdešimt penktaisiais metais.",
          "gloss": "I was born in 1995."
        },
        {
          "target": "Du tūkstančiai dvidešimtaisiais metais.",
          "gloss": "In the year 2020."
        }
      ],
      "footnotes": [
        "In speech the whole phrase is often cut down to the last word: *devyniasdešimt penktaisiais*, in ninety-five. The biographical uses of years and age — *Man … metų*, full birth dates, *prieš … metus* — are taken up in the next section (¶88–¶92)."
      ],
      "seeAlso": [
        "ordinals",
        "instrumental-time-route",
        "cardinals-ten-up"
      ],
      "core": false
    },
    {
      "id": "time-prepositions",
      "number": "87",
      "heading": "Prepositions of Time",
      "statement": "Three prepositions of time take the **accusative** where those of ¶33 took the genitive. **Prieš** is *ago* or *before*; **per** is *within* a stretch or *during* it. Against them stand the genitive pair **nuo … iki**, from one time to another, which frames a working day or an opening hour.",
      "paradigms": [
        {
          "caption": "Time prepositions and their cases",
          "columns": [
            "preposition",
            "case",
            "example"
          ],
          "rows": [
            {
              "label": "prieš",
              "cells": [
                "accusative",
                "prieš valandą — an hour ago"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "per",
              "cells": [
                "accusative",
                "per valandą — within an hour"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "po",
              "cells": [
                "genitive",
                "po pietų — after lunch"
              ]
            },
            {
              "label": "nuo … iki",
              "cells": [
                "genitive",
                "nuo aštuntos iki penktos — from eight to five"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "target": "Prieš metus atvažiavau į Lietuvą.",
          "gloss": "I came to Lithuania a year ago."
        },
        {
          "target": "Per valandą viską padarysiu.",
          "gloss": "I shall do everything within an hour."
        },
        {
          "target": "Nuo šiandien iki penktadienio nedirbu.",
          "gloss": "From today until Friday I am not working."
        }
      ],
      "seeAlso": [
        "genitive-prepositions",
        "accusative-of-time",
        "instrumental-po"
      ],
      "core": true
    }
  ],
